# tools/color_contrast_witness.rish -- a WCAG contrast table read over a whole on-colour palette proves itself (Season G).
#
# Season G (Open Media Primitives) -- the accessibility table beside the on-colour swatch (image/color_swatch.rye), the
# tonal scale (image/color_scale.rye), the palette toolkit (image/color_adjust.rye), and the open colour algebra
# (image/color.rye).
# Design read: active-designing/20260816-210735_season-g-color-algebra-crux.md (the colour floor this stands on).
# Teacher, thanked clean-room: gratitude/w3c-css-color.md (the W3C CSS Color spec + WCAG contrast -- public standards only).
#
# The crux this witness proves is the table a design system ships beside its colours: for every swatch of an on-colour
# palette, the exact WCAG contrast of its ink against its fill and which conformance bar that ink clears (AA-large,
# AA-normal, AAA). Written as a single-stranded consumer -- color_swatch DECIDES each fill-and-ink pair, color MEASURES
# each contrast, this module only READS one measurement per swatch. Every reading agrees byte-for-byte with color's own
# contrast_ratio_x100 and meets_aa/meets_aaa; the three bars nest every row; this blue ramp clears AA-normal on every
# tone; and the report is HONEST -- a deliberately low-contrast grey-on-grey swatch reads below AA-normal and the table
# says so, so it reports illegible pairs as faithfully as legible ones. No new storage, codec, or maths. No network, no
# key, no funds.
#
# Run from the repository root:
#   rishi/bin/rishi run tools/color_contrast_witness.rish

say "color-contrast: Language EN -- Season G's accessibility table; a keeper reads back not just an on-colour palette but a proof of which tones are legible body text, which need large text, and which reach the AAA bar."
say "color-contrast: Style Radiant -- compose not braid; color_swatch DECIDES each fill-and-ink pair and color MEASURES each contrast, so a reading is a pure read over the two existing verbs, both modules' proofs carried through."
say "color-contrast: Lens TAME -- u32 ratios on the x100 scale bounded 100..2100; every report one reading per swatch, bounded by report_max_tones; a length mismatch refused by name; honest about failing rows; no network, no key, no funds."

let zig = "vendor/zig-toolchain/zig"
let bin = "image/bin/color_contrast"

let build = run ["sh" "-c" "mkdir -p image/bin && env RYE_ZIG=${zig} rye/bin/rye build image/color_contrast.rye -femit-bin=${bin}"]
assert build.ok else "color-contrast: build failed -- ${build.err}"

let selftest = run ["sh" "-c" "${bin} selftest 2>&1"]
assert selftest.ok else "color-contrast: selftest exited non-zero -- ${selftest.out}"

let out = trim selftest.out
say "color-contrast: ${out}"

# Honour the loom REDS %76 named: check every claim with Rishi's native `contains`, never a shell grep over interpolated
# output, so an apostrophe in the selftest prose (here "swatch's ink") can never break a check.
assert out contains "GREEN image-color-contrast" else "color-contrast: selftest did not print the GREEN colour-contrast line"
assert out contains "agreeing byte-for-byte with color.contrast_ratio_x100" else "color-contrast: a reading did not agree with color's own measurement"
assert out contains "the three conformance bars nest every row" else "color-contrast: the AA-large / AA-normal / AAA bars did not nest"
assert out contains "clears the AA-normal bar (450) on every one of its nine tones" else "color-contrast: the blue ramp did not clear AA-normal on every tone"
assert out contains "reads below AA-normal and the table says so plainly" else "color-contrast: the report did not honestly report a failing row"
assert out contains "refuses ReportLenMismatch by name" else "color-contrast: a length mismatch was not refused by name"

say "color-contrast: GREEN -- the WCAG contrast table over a whole on-colour palette whole; each reading measures its own swatch, the bars nest, the ramp clears AA, a failing row is reported honestly, a length mismatch refused, determinism proven."
